{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block page_title %}Exchequer{% endblock %}

{% block description %}The District's Exchequer: the debt it manages, how long the District borrows for, and what the debt costs.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="max-w-400 mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-8 pb-12 w-full space-y-6">

	{% embed 'government/_header.html.twig' with {title: 'Exchequer'} %}
		{% block lead %}
			The District's treasury. It carries out the budget the Diet passes and funds it, selling bills repaid within the
			year and bonds that run for decades. Its head is named by the Aerie Council for a single term and decides how long
			the District borrows for.
		{% endblock %}
	{% endembed %}

	{% if exchequer %}
		{% embed 'government/_head.html.twig' with {head: exchequer.head} %}
			{% block stance -%}
				{{ head.stanceText }},
				{{ head.opening ? 'keeping the debt at the average maturity it had at Year 1' : 'steering the debt toward an average maturity of' }}
				{%- if not head.opening %} <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ head.maturity|number_format(1) }}</span> years{% endif %}
			{%- endblock %}
			{% block candidate %}<span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ candidate.maturity|number_format(1) }}</span> years, {% endblock %}
			{% block rules %}
				The Council names the head for a single {{ exchequer.rules.termYears|number_format(0) }}-year term from a shortlist of {{ exchequer.rules.shortlist }}, choosing the candidate nearest its own view of the debt.
				{% if exchequer.councilMaturity is not null %}The Council's median member would borrow at <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.councilMaturity|number_format(1) }}</span> years on average.{% endif %}
			{% endblock %}
		{% endembed %}

		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
			<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="debt-heading">
				<h2 id="debt-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">The debt</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold font-mono tabular-nums text-on-surface">{{ exchequer.debt|pct(1) }}</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">of GDP, <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.netDebt|pct(1) }}</span> net of the bonds the Sovereign Reserve Fund holds. {% if exchequer.netLiabilities >= 0 %}Set against everything the state holds, it owes <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.netLiabilities|pct(1) }}</span>{% else %}The state holds <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ (-exchequer.netLiabilities)|pct(1) }}</span> of GDP more than it owes{% endif %}</p>
				<dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-3 mt-4 text-xs">
					<div>
						<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">Average maturity</dt>
						<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5"><span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.maturity|number_format(1) }}</span> years{% if exchequer.movingTo is not null %}, {{ exchequer.movingTo > exchequer.maturity ? 'lengthening' : 'shortening' }} toward <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.movingTo|number_format(1) }}</span>{% endif %}</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">Repriced within the year</dt>
						<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5 font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.repricingShare|pct(0) }}</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">Average rate paid</dt>
						<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5 font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.rate|pct(2) }}</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">Interest a year</dt>
						<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5"><span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.interestToGdp|pct(1) }}</span> of GDP</dd>
					</div>
					<div class="col-span-2">
						<dt class="text-on-surface-variant">Paid in by the Monetary Authority</dt>
						<dd class="text-on-surface mt-0.5">{% if exchequer.authorityLossesToGdp > 0 %}Nothing until it has made up <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.authorityLossesToGdp|pct(1) }}</span> of GDP in losses{% else %}<span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.remittanceToGdp|pct(2) }}</span> of GDP a year, its profit on the currency and the bonds it holds{% endif %}</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-4 leading-relaxed">
					Bills and maturing bonds are refinanced at the rates of the day, so a shorter debt passes a change in the policy rate into the budget sooner.
					The debt reaches a new average maturity only as it rolls over, over several years.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="bg-surface-container-low rounded-lg p-5 border border-outline-variant/20" aria-labelledby="market-heading">
				<h2 id="market-heading" class="text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface">The bond market</h2>
				<p class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold font-mono tabular-nums text-on-surface">{{ exchequer.tenYear|pct(2) }}</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant">ten-year yield</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface mt-3">
					{%- set bp = exchequer.maturityBp -%}
					{%- set points = bp|abs == 1 ? ' basis point' : ' basis points' -%}
					{% if bp == 0 %}
						The debt's maturity adds nothing to the ten-year against a debt of <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.rules.founding|number_format(1) }}</span> years.
					{% else %}
						The debt's maturity {{ bp > 0 ? 'adds' : 'takes' }} about <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ bp|abs }}</span>{{ points }} {{ bp > 0 ? 'to' : 'off' }} the ten-year against a debt of <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.rules.founding|number_format(1) }}</span> years.
					{% endif %}
				</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					Long bonds leave pension funds, insurers and banks more interest-rate risk to carry, and they ask to be paid for it.
					A longer debt locks in today's rates and costs more while long rates sit above short ones; a shorter one is cheaper until rates rise.
					A head may steer anywhere from {{ exchequer.rules.shortest|number_format(1) }} to {{ exchequer.rules.longest|number_format(1) }} years.
				</p>
				<p class="text-xs text-on-surface-variant mt-3 leading-relaxed">
					Lenders also charge for the chance the District does not repay, now <span class="font-mono tabular-nums">{{ exchequer.riskSpreadBp }}</span> {{ exchequer.riskSpreadBp|abs == 1 ? 'basis point' : 'basis points' }} on every bond it sells.
					The charge is small while what the state owes is well covered by what it holds, and climbs steeply as its net debt rises.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	{% else %}
		<p class="text-sm text-on-surface-variant">The Exchequer has no head yet.</p>
	{% endif %}

	<p class="source-note">{{ source_line('exchequer') }}</p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
